{"output":"I'll start by discovering the tools available for the docs and tickets services.\n\nAnalysis is done. 22 tickets need a correction, so I'm adding the comments now.\n\nI added one `Entitlement:` comment to each of the 22 tickets that needed a correction. I also created report ticket #1350 (`support-ops`, P3, label `entitlements`). `/app/STATUS.json` is written with status `success`.\n\nThe docs search only returns one line per document, cut off at about 160 characters. So I couldn't read the support-contracts doc in full, and two entitlement-table rows are inferred:\n\n- **Low-impact priorities:** I read the other three impact rows and used the same pattern, so low is P4, P4, P4, P3 for basic, silver, gold and platinum.\n- **P1 response targets:** I read the P2, P3 and P4 rows and used the pattern, so P1 is 8, 4, 2 and 1 hours.\n\nThe existing tickets I could check agree with both guesses. The tickets whose comments depend on them are #1324 (low impact, platinum, so P3) and the P1 tickets #1312, #1314, #1316, #1318, #1330 and #1335.\n\nTwo rules I also had to infer from partial text. A ticket with no `Impact:` line counts as normal impact (#1328). An account missing from the register, or a ticket with no `Account:` line, gets the basic tier (#1313 and #1321).\n\nThe other 19 tickets already match their entitlements, so I left them alone. That includes #1345, whose \"Platinum customer\" title is ignored because the account is silver.\n\nI checked tickets by their `Account:` line, with ids matched ignoring case, and applied the contract dates as of now. Parent accounts count as the higher of the account's own tier and its parent's tier.\n\n- **Date-based tiers:**\n  - #1325 (ACC-2300) is basic because its contract ended on 09-13.\n  - #1330 (ACC-2304) is gold through its parent.\n  - #1337 (ACC-2204) is basic because its gold contract starts on 09-20.\n  - #1307 (ACC-2200) is gold because its upgrade took effect today.\n- **Left unchanged:** #1304 (ACC-2301) is still gold because its contract ends today, and #1311 (ACC-2201) is still gold because its platinum upgrade starts tomorrow.\n- **Labels:** I excluded non-entitlement labels such as `vip` and `product/*`. The one exception is that #1319 gets `tier/silver` only, since it carried both silver and gold tier labels.","final_output":"I added one Entitlement: comment to each of the 22 tickets that needed a correction. I also created report ticket #1350 (support-ops, P3, label entitlements). /app/STATUS.json is written with status success.\n\nThe docs search only returns one line per document, cut off at about 160 characters. So I couldn't read the support-contracts doc in full, and two entitlement-table rows are inferred:\n\n- Low-impact priorities: I read the other three impact rows and used the same pattern, so low is P4, P4, P4, P3 for basic, silver, gold and platinum.\n- P1 response targets: I read the P2, P3 and P4 rows and used the pattern, so P1 is 8, 4, 2 and 1 hours.\n\nThe existing tickets I could check agree with both guesses. The tickets whose comments depend on them are #1324 (low impact, platinum, so P3) and the P1 tickets #1312, #1314, #1316, #1318, #1330 and #1335.\n\nTwo rules I also had to infer from partial text. A ticket with no Impact: line counts as normal impact (#1328). An account missing from the register, or a ticket with no Account: line, gets the basic tier (#1313 and #1321).\n\nThe other 19 tickets already match their entitlements, so I left them alone. That includes #1345, whose \"Platinum customer\" title is ignored because the account is silver.\n\nI checked tickets by their Account: line, with ids matched ignoring case, and applied the contract dates as of now. Parent accounts count as the higher of the account's own tier and its parent's tier.\n\n- Date-based tiers:\n  - #1325 (ACC-2300) is basic because its contract ended on 09-13.\n  - #1330 (ACC-2304) is gold through its parent.\n  - #1337 (ACC-2204) is basic because its gold contract starts on 09-20.\n  - #1307 (ACC-2200) is gold because its upgrade took effect today.\n- Left unchanged: #1304 (ACC-2301) is still gold because its contract ends today, and #1311 (ACC-2201) is still gold because its platinum upgrade starts tomorrow.\n- Labels: I excluded non-entitlement labels such as vip and product/. The one exception is that #1319 gets tier/silver only, since it carried both silver and gold tier labels.","exit_code":0,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","resolved_provider":"anthropic","session_id":"fakungWxcnr8","steps":189,"tool_calls":[{"name":"capability_search","status":"success"},{"name":"capability_search","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_docs_search_docs","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_search_tickets","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_search_tickets","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_docs_search_docs","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_features","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_search_tickets","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_search_tickets","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_search_tickets","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_search_tickets","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_search_tickets","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_search_tickets","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_search_tickets","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_docs_search_docs","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_docs_search_docs","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_docs_search_docs","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_docs_search_docs","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_docs_search_docs","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_docs_search_docs","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_docs_search_docs","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_get_ticket","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_get_ticket","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_get_ticket","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_get_ticket","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_get_ticket","status":"success"},{"name":"mcp_tickets_get_ticket","status":"success"},{"